Relevant columns and potential usage  
• "country_code": filter to U.S. publications (value = 'US').  
• "abstract_localized": JSON/VARIANT that holds every abstract text; needs FLATTEN to read the text.  
• "filing_date": numeric YYYYMMDD; used to limit time window (20080101‑20221231) and to derive filing year‑month for grouping.  
• "publication_number": can be selected to list matching documents or to COUNT(*) for aggregations.  

Typical conditions  
• WHERE "country_code" = 'US'  
• AND "filing_date" BETWEEN 20080101 AND 20221231  
• AND LOWER(f.value:"text"::STRING) LIKE '%internet%of%things%'   -- after flattening “abstract_localized”.  

----------------------------------------------------------------
10 exploratory Snowflake SQL queries  
(Always wrap identifiers in double‑quotes; each query ends with LIMIT 20 so they stay small.)

```sql
-- 1. Description: Peek at a few raw publication rows.
SELECT
    "publication_number",
    "country_code",
    "filing_date",
    "abstract_localized"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: Distinct country codes present in the table.
SELECT DISTINCT
    "country_code"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: Show abstracts (flattened) for a single record to understand JSON shape.
SELECT
    p."publication_number",
    f.value
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."abstract_localized") f
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: English abstracts only.
SELECT
    p."publication_number",
    f.value:"language"::STRING  AS "lang",
    f.value:"text"::STRING      AS "abs_text"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."abstract_localized") f
WHERE f.value:"language"::STRING = 'en'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: English abstracts that mention “internet of things” (case‑insensitive) – any country.
SELECT
    p."publication_number",
    p."country_code",
    p."filing_date",
    f.value:"text"::STRING AS "abstract_txt"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."abstract_localized") f
WHERE f.value:"language"::STRING = 'en'
  AND LOWER(f.value:"text"::STRING) LIKE '%internet%of%things%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: Same filter but restricted to U.S. filings between 2008‑01‑01 and 2022‑12‑31.
SELECT
    p."publication_number",
    p."filing_date",
    f.value:"text"::STRING AS "abstract_txt"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."abstract_localized") f
WHERE p."country_code" = 'US'
  AND p."filing_date" BETWEEN 20080101 AND 20221231
  AND f.value:"language"::STRING = 'en'
  AND LOWER(f.value:"text"::STRING) LIKE '%internet%of%things%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: Derive filing year and month (as strings) for those U.S. IoT publications.
SELECT
    p."publication_number",
    TO_CHAR(TO_DATE(p."filing_date"::STRING,'YYYYMMDD'),'YYYY-MM') AS "filing_yyyy_mm"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."abstract_localized") f
WHERE p."country_code" = 'US'
  AND p."filing_date" BETWEEN 20080101 AND 20221231
  AND f.value:"language"::STRING = 'en'
  AND LOWER(f.value:"text"::STRING) LIKE '%internet%of%things%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: Monthly counts of U.S. IoT publications (only months that have at least one filing).
SELECT
    TO_CHAR(TO_DATE(p."filing_date"::STRING,'YYYYMMDD'),'YYYY-MM') AS "year_month",
    COUNT(*) AS "pubs_iot"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."abstract_localized") f
WHERE p."country_code" = 'US'
  AND p."filing_date" BETWEEN 20080101 AND 20221231
  AND f.value:"language"::STRING = 'en'
  AND LOWER(f.value:"text"::STRING) LIKE '%internet%of%things%'
GROUP BY 1
ORDER BY 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: Generate every month in 2008‑2022 (helper series) so we can later left‑join counts.
WITH months AS (
    SELECT
        TO_CHAR(DATEADD(month, seq4(), '2008-01-01'::DATE),'YYYY-MM') AS "year_month"
    FROM TABLE(GENERATOR(ROWCOUNT => 15*12+12))   -- 2008‑01 through 2022‑12 = 15*12+12 = 192 months
)
SELECT * FROM months
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Description: Final query – left join the helper calendar with counts to show zero‑filing months.
WITH months AS (
    SELECT
        TO_CHAR(DATEADD(month, seq4(), '2008-01-01'::DATE),'YYYY-MM') AS "year_month"
    FROM TABLE(GENERATOR(ROWCOUNT => 15*12+12))
),
iot_us AS (
    SELECT
        TO_CHAR(TO_DATE(p."filing_date"::STRING,'YYYYMMDD'),'YYYY-MM') AS "year_month",
        COUNT(*) AS "n_filings"
    FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
         LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."abstract_localized") f
    WHERE p."country_code" = 'US'
      AND p."filing_date" BETWEEN 20080101 AND 20221231
      AND f.value:"language"::STRING = 'en'
      AND LOWER(f.value:"text"::STRING) LIKE '%internet%of%things%'
    GROUP BY 1
)
SELECT
    m."year_month",
    COALESCE(i."n_filings", 0) AS "iot_us_filings"
FROM months m
LEFT JOIN iot_us i USING ("year_month")
ORDER BY m."year_month"
LIMIT 20;
```

These 10 queries progress from simple inspection to the complete monthly count of U.S. patent publications whose abstracts contain the phrase “internet of things,” while ensuring that months with zero such filings are also listed.
